If someone's phone number changes tomorrow, an old job can still retain evidence that the contact number used on that job was the number valid at that time without corrupting the historical record.

7. Access control should be both role-based and job-based

LeaseOS shouldn't ask only:

Is this person a Driver?

It should ask:

Who is requesting this?
        +
Which company?
        +
What role?
        +
What job?
        +
Are they assigned to that job?
        +
What classification is this contact method?
        =
Allowed fields

So a driver requesting:

GET /jobs/26-00982/contacts

might receive:

assigned dispatcher
client representative
consultant
medic
disposal
ERAP
emergency contacts

The same driver requesting:

GET /organizations/client-A/all-employees

gets:

DENIED

That fail-closed model fits LeaseOS very well.

