And importantly, an ERAP telephone number should come from the actual shipment/job documentation, rather than LeaseOS assuming there is a universal ERAP number.

Transport Canada says every ERAP has its own ERAP telephone number and, when a consignment requires an ERAP, that number appears on the shipping document. 

LeaseOS should therefore connect:

Dangerous Goods Manifest
        ↓
UN / commodity determination
        ↓
ERAP required?
        ↓
ERAP reference
ERAP holder
ERAP telephone
        ↓
Job Emergency Directory

That is a really useful integration with the TDG work we've already discussed.

11. CANUTEC can be a verified system contact

Transport Canada currently directs people dealing with a dangerous-goods release or anticipated release to the appropriate local authority, CANUTEC, and—when applicable—the ERAP holder identified on the shipping document. 

That means LeaseOS can maintain system-managed verified emergency records, separate from tenant-entered contacts.

I would distinguish them visually:

✓ LeaseOS Verified — Government Source

versus

Company supplied — verified Sep. 15, 2026

That prevents someone accidentally editing an official number and propagating a bad number across the fleet.

12. Offline operation is essential

Current-job contact information should be bundled into the offline job package:

Job
Route
Manifest
TDG
ERAP
Safety forms
Job contacts
Emergency contacts

Then if the driver loses internet on a lease road, they still have the numbers.

But LeaseOS should not download the company's entire workforce database onto every driver's phone.

Cache only what the user is authorized to use:

Current jobs
Recent assigned-job contacts
Required company contacts
Required emergency directory

Encrypt that data locally and invalidate it when the assignment/account changes.

13. This also gives the AI secretary a much better model

Instead of the AI having arbitrary access to phone numbers, the AI asks the contact service:

Who is the disposal contact for this job?

Contact service:

User: driver_82
Job: 26-00982
Authorized: yes

Jane Doe
Secure Disposal – Fox Creek
Role: Scale House
780-...

Then the AI could say:

“Secure Fox Creek's scale-house contact is Jane Doe. Do you want me to open the dialer?”

The AI should never receive unrestricted contact-directory access if it doesn't need it.

14. It also addresses the privacy concern you raised

Alberta PIPA applies to many private-sector businesses and limits collection of personal information to reasonable purposes and to what is reasonably needed for those purposes. Organizations also have obligations to protect the personal information they hold. 

Your instinct to avoid pulling workers' personal phone contacts into LeaseOS is therefore the right architectural direction.

